1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,071
Chai Corner now has five
outlets and a small head office.

2
00:00:04,371 --> 00:00:07,709
And every day, forty
questions land on Ravi's desk.

3
00:00:08,259 --> 00:00:10,908
Milk is running low at outlet three.

4
00:00:10,908 --> 00:00:11,808
Ask Ravi.

5
00:00:12,088 --> 00:00:14,215
A customer wants a refund.

6
00:00:14,215 --> 00:00:15,159
Ask Ravi.

7
00:00:15,459 --> 00:00:18,512
And a big new chai shop
just opened next door.

8
00:00:18,512 --> 00:00:20,916
Ravi has no time left for that one.

9
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:23,825
Not every decision needs the boss.

10
00:00:23,825 --> 00:00:25,439
He needs to sort them.

11
00:00:26,139 --> 00:00:28,104
So, how do we sort decisions?

12
00:00:28,404 --> 00:00:32,961
In 1960, the thinker Herbert
Simon split them into two types.

13
00:00:33,361 --> 00:00:36,440
Programmed decisions are
repetitive and routine.

14
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:39,808
Non-programmed decisions
are new, and unstructured.

15
00:00:40,458 --> 00:00:42,790
Let's start with programmed decisions.

16
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:46,681
They come up again and again,
so you can write a rule once.

17
00:00:47,031 --> 00:00:47,931
Rule one.

18
00:00:47,809 --> 00:00:50,874
When milk falls below
twenty litres, reorder it.

19
00:00:51,224 --> 00:00:52,124
Rule two.

20
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:54,514
A wrong order gets a full refund.

21
00:00:54,864 --> 00:00:56,700
This is called a procedure.

22
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,681
Fixed steps anyone can follow.

23
00:00:59,031 --> 00:01:02,427
So these go to lower levels,
like Meena at outlet two.

24
00:01:02,427 --> 00:01:03,690
Quick, and cheap.

25
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,457
Now, non-programmed decisions.

26
00:01:06,857 --> 00:01:09,491
These are new, and they come up rarely.

27
00:01:09,491 --> 00:01:10,515
No rule fits.

28
00:01:10,865 --> 00:01:13,879
Should Chai Corner open
an outlet in another city?

29
00:01:14,229 --> 00:01:16,763
How should it answer
the new shop next door?

30
00:01:17,113 --> 00:01:20,275
They need judgment, that
means weighing the facts.

31
00:01:20,275 --> 00:01:22,164
And creativity, fresh ideas.

32
00:01:22,514 --> 00:01:24,722
So these go to the top, to Ravi.

33
00:01:24,722 --> 00:01:25,985
They matter a lot.

34
00:01:26,635 --> 00:01:30,106
Now Ravi plays a sorting
game with today's questions.

35
00:01:30,506 --> 00:01:31,666
Reorder milk.

36
00:01:31,666 --> 00:01:32,644
Programmed.

37
00:01:32,944 --> 00:01:33,910
A refund.

38
00:01:33,910 --> 00:01:34,922
Programmed.

39
00:01:35,222 --> 00:01:36,334
A new city.

40
00:01:36,334 --> 00:01:37,480
Non-programmed.

41
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:39,544
The new shop next door.

42
00:01:39,544 --> 00:01:40,592
Non-programmed.

43
00:01:40,942 --> 00:01:43,918
Thirty-six of forty
land in the routine bin.

44
00:01:43,918 --> 00:01:45,509
Ravi keeps just four.

45
00:01:46,159 --> 00:01:48,566
Side by side, the difference is clear.

46
00:01:48,916 --> 00:01:53,245
Programmed decisions are routine,
made with rules, at lower levels.

47
00:01:53,595 --> 00:01:57,645
Non-programmed decisions are new,
made with judgment, at the top.

48
00:01:57,995 --> 00:02:02,010
Rules handle the routine, so the
boss has time for what is new.

49
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:03,560
Quick check.

50
00:02:03,536 --> 00:02:07,595
A storm shuts the dairy for a week,
and nothing like this has happened

51
00:02:07,595 --> 00:02:08,495
before.

52
00:02:08,192 --> 00:02:10,145
Which type of decision is this?

53
00:02:12,045 --> 00:02:13,017
Non-programmed!

54
00:02:13,017 --> 00:02:16,493
It is new, there is no
rule, so it needs judgment.

55
00:02:17,093 --> 00:02:18,106
So, remember.

56
00:02:18,406 --> 00:02:21,809
Programmed decisions are
routine, and made with rules.

57
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:26,529
Non-programmed decisions are new,
and need judgment and creativity.

58
00:02:26,879 --> 00:02:28,865
Routine goes to lower levels.

59
00:02:28,865 --> 00:02:30,921
New and big goes to the top.

60
00:02:31,521 --> 00:02:33,934
Next time, rational decision making.

61
00:02:33,934 --> 00:02:36,218
How to pick the very best option.
